  ["Commercial property", ["Office, retail, industrial, and multifamily buildings can offer larger income and longer leases, but they usually require more capital, expertise, and risk tolerance. Many investors reach commercial property through partnerships or REITs."]],
  ["REITs", ["A real estate investment trust (REIT) owns or finances income-producing property. REITs must generally distribute at least 90% of their taxable income to shareholders, so they often pay higher dividends. Publicly traded REITs can be bought like stocks, and REIT index funds hold many at once."]],
