 fit=dict(starter="Practice the four Ms on companies you use every day.", mom="Teach your children to ask: do I understand this business?", rebuilder="Use the four Ms to evaluate any investment you are offered.", ent="Ask what moat your own business is building.", exec="Apply the four Ms to your employer honestly.", late="Use the four Ms to keep individual picks high quality.", retiree="Favor companies with wide moats and steady management.", legacy="The four Ms are a lasting framework to pass on."),
 example="Brenda applies the four Ms to a payment company. Meaning: she uses it and understands its fees. Moat: millions of merchants and users create a network effect. Management: the founders own large stakes and their letters match their actions. Margin of safety: the stock trades near her estimate of value, not below it, so she adds it to her watch list instead of buying today. (Hypothetical example.)",
 terms=[["Meaning", "Understanding a business and its alignment with your values."], ["Moat", "A lasting competitive advantage."], ["Network effect", "When a product becomes more valuable as more people use it."], ["Switching costs", "The difficulty for customers to change providers."], ["Management", "The leaders running the company."], ["Margin of safety", "Buying meaningfully below estimated value."]],
